A couple thoughts that I had:

cheepicus@hotmail.com wrote:
> * HP/SP cap
> The cap would be a bit soft. HP/SP max over the cap would drift
> down towards it at a speed proportional to your healing rate. But
> slow enough where someone could enjoy having huge HP for awhile
> if they really wanted to. Race and class big inputs to the cap.

Assuming that this patch is intended to be relevant to moderately
experienced players, the cap would have to be pretty low -- 150
HP would probably be the top.  Once a player has ascended a couple
times, having 1000 HP is no better than 200 HP, so setting the cap
high would have no effect.

> * Diminishing returns on negative AC.
> Leaning towards: DR = min(min(rnd(-ac),rnd(-ac)),20).

I'm too lazy to find exact numbers for the damage reduction, but
I put together a script to calculate the damage reduction for
different AC.  The results are below.  I notice a couple
things:

- This formula doesn't just give diminishing returns for very low 
  AC; it also changes the amount of damage reduction quite 
  substantially -- for the first 25 points or so, you essentially
  get about 1/3 of a point of reduction (average) compared to
  Nethack's current formula.

  That means that you would either live with taking more damage
  at a given AC level, or you would have to pump up your AC beyond
  what you would in the current nethack.  For instance, if you
  currently are comfortable at AC:-20, then to get the equivalent
  protection with the new formula, you would need somewhere in
  the neighborhood of AC:-31.  That's a pretty dramatic jump.
  Looking at it from the other direction, an AC:-20 in the new system
  is equivalent to about AC:-13 in the current system -- which is
  rather high for an ascension, in my opinion.

  I would be concerned that this change would actually lead people
  to spend more time beefing up their AC, which I think is the opposite
  of what you intend.

- The diminishing returns don't really become serious until somewhere
  in the -30s.  (At AC:-30, you're still getting about 0.25 points
  of damage reduction per point of AC).  Since AC below -30 or so
  is kind of pointless anyway, this really doesn't have much of an
  effect.

